{"sounds":{"intro":"Romanian is written in the Latin alphabet and is a Romance language, so many words look like Italian or Spanish. It is spelled almost exactly as it sounds. Nouns are masculine, feminine or neuter. The stress is usually on the second-to-last syllable.","rows":[["ă","a short, flat \"uh\", like the \"a\" in \"about\"","casă"],["â / î","a deep, throaty \"uh\", said far back in the mouth","România, în"],["ș","sh, like \"ship\"","șase"],["ț","ts, like \"ts\" in \"cats\"","mulțumesc"],["c (before e, i)","ch, like \"church\"","cinci"],["ch / gh (before e, i)","\"k\" and \"g\", as in \"king\" and \"get\"","chei, ghid"],["e (at the start)","\"ye\" in some words","este"]],"notes":["\"c\" before e or i is \"ch\", and \"g\" before e or i is \"j\". To get a hard \"c\" or \"g\" before e or i, Romanian writes \"ch\" or \"gh\".","\"i\" at the end of a word is often almost silent. It softens the consonant before it: lupi (lups)."]},"numbers":[{"id":"0-to-10","title":"0 to 10","items":[["zero","zero","ZEH-roh"],["one","unu","OO-noo"],["two","doi","doy"],["three","trei","tray"],["four","patru","PAH-troo"],["five","cinci","cheench"],["six","șase","SHAH-seh"],["seven","șapte","SHAHP-teh"],["eight","opt","opt"],["nine","nouă","NOH-uh"],["ten","zece","ZEH-cheh"]]},{"id":"11-to-20","title":"11 to 20","items":[["eleven","unsprezece","OON-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["twelve","doisprezece","DOY-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["thirteen","treisprezece","TRAY-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["fourteen","paisprezece","PIE-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["fifteen","cincisprezece","CHEENCH-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["sixteen","șaisprezece","SHAI-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["seventeen","șaptesprezece","SHAHP-teh-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["eighteen","optsprezece","OPT-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["nineteen","nouăsprezece","NOH-uh-spreh-zeh-cheh"],["twenty","douăzeci","DOH-uh-zech"]]},{"id":"tens","title":"Tens","items":[["ten","zece","ZEH-cheh"],["twenty","douăzeci","DOH-uh-zech"],["thirty","treizeci","tray-ZECH"],["forty","patruzeci","pah-troo-ZECH"],["fifty","cincizec